<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net"><diagram name="Data Model" id="prox-data"><mxGraphModel dx="1900" dy="1300" grid="1" gridSize="10" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1900" pageHeight="1300" background="#ffffff"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
<mxCell id="t" value="PROXIMITY SEARCH - Data Model (PostgreSQL PostGIS + Elasticsearch + Redis Geo + Kafka)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;fontSize=20;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1a237e" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="20" width="1740" height="35" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="pgLabel" value="POSTGRESQL + PostGIS (Source of Truth)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#e1bee7;align=left;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#7b1fa2;rounded=1;strokeWidth=2;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="70" width="900" height="35" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="places" value="TABLE: places\n\nplace_id          BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY\nname              VARCHAR(200) NOT NULL\ncategory          VARCHAR(50) -- restaurant, hotel, gas_station\nrating            NUMERIC(2,1) -- 0.0 to 5.0\naddress           TEXT\ncity              VARCHAR(100)\ncountry_code      CHAR(2)\nphone             VARCHAR(20)\nlocation          GEOGRAPHY(POINT, 4326) NOT NULL -- WGS 84\ngeohash           CHAR(12) -- precomputed for sharding\nopen_hours        JSONB\nphoto_urls        TEXT[]\ncreated_at        TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()\nupdated_at        TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()\n\nINDEXES:\n  CREATE INDEX idx_location_gist ON places USING GIST(location); -- R-tree spatial index\n  CREATE INDEX idx_category ON places(category); -- for filters\n  CREATE INDEX idx_geohash ON places(geohash); -- for sharding\n  CREATE INDEX idx_city_category ON places(city, category); -- composite for common query\n\nQUERY EXAMPLE:\n  SELECT place_id, name, ST_Distance(location, user_point) AS dist_m\n  FROM places\n  WHERE category = 'restaurant'\n    AND ST_DWithin(location, ST_GeogFromText('POINT(77.59 12.97)'), 5000)\n  ORDER BY location &lt;-&gt; ST_GeogFromText('POINT(77.59 12.97)') -- KNN distance operator\n  LIMIT 50;\n\nSHARDING: By region (US-West DB, EU DB) or geohash prefix (9q8 → shard 1, dr5 → shard 2) with 10km overlap." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=monospace" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="120" width="900" height="450" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="reviews" value="TABLE: reviews\n\nreview_id       BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY\nplace_id        BIGINT REFERENCES places(place_id) ON DELETE CASCADE\nuser_id         BIGINT NOT NULL\nrating          SMALLINT CHECK (rating BETWEEN 1 AND 5)\ncomment         TEXT\nphoto_urls      TEXT[]\ncreated_at      TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()\n\nINDEXES:\n  CREATE INDEX idx_place_id ON reviews(place_id);\n  CREATE INDEX idx_created_at ON reviews(created_at DESC);" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=monospace" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="590" width="550" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="esLabel" value="ELASTICSEARCH (Search + Filter Layer)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#fff9c4;align=left;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#f57f17;rounded=1;strokeWidth=2;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="980" y="70" width="880" height="35" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="esMapping" value="INDEX: places&#10;&#10;MAPPING (geo_point field type)&#10;location: {type: geo_point} ⭐ BKD tree index&#10;name: {type: text}&#10;category: {type: keyword}&#10;rating: {type: half_float}&#10;&#10;QUERY EXAMPLE:&#10;geo_distance filter + term filters + match text&#10;distance: 5km from (12.97, 77.59)&#10;category: restaurant&#10;rating gte 4&#10;name match: pizza&#10;sort by _geo_distance asc&#10;&#10;Combines proximity + text search + filters in single query&#10;&#10;SHARDING: 5-10 shards per 100M documents. Route by city or geohash prefix." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffde7;strokeColor=#f57f17;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=monospace" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="980" y="120" width="880" height="450" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="redisLabel" value="REDIS GEO (Hot Cache + Real-Time)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#ffebee;align=left;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#c62828;rounded=1;strokeWidth=2;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="980" y="590" width="880" height="35" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="redisKeys" value="REDIS GEOSPATIAL DATA STRUCTURES&#10;&#10;1. GEORADIUS for proximity:&#10;   Key: drivers:online (Uber/Lyft drivers)&#10;   Type: Sorted Set (ZSET) with geohash as score&#10;   Commands:&#10;     GEOADD drivers:online 77.59 12.97 driver_12345&#10;     GEORADIUS drivers:online 77.59 12.97 5 km WITHDIST ASC COUNT 10&#10;     GEORADIUSBYMEMBER drivers:online driver_12345 2 km&#10;   Encoding: ~50 bytes/point &#10;   1M drivers ≈ 50 MB&#10;   TTL: 10 min (drivers ping every 5s, GEOADD upserts)&#10;&#10;2. Hot place cache (query result cache):&#10;   Key: search:{lat}:{lng}:{radius}:{category}:{filters_hash}&#10;   Value: JSON array with place_id, dist_m, name&#10;   TTL: 10 min (static places change rarely)&#10;   Example: SET search:12.97:77.59:5:restaurant:rating_4 EX 600&#10;&#10;3. Place metadata cache:&#10;   Key: place:{place_id}&#10;   Value: JSON with name, address, hours, photo_urls, rating&#10;   TTL: 1 hour (write-through on updates)&#10;   Example: GET place:12345 returns metadata JSON&#10;&#10;NOTE: Boundary edge case (query center cell + 8 geohash neighbors) is handled at query time by generating 9 geohash prefixes and issuing 9 lookups (SQL LIKE or ES terms filter) — not a separate cached Redis structure." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffebee;strokeColor=#c62828;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=monospace" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="980" y="640" width="880" height="370" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="kafkaLabel" value="KAFKA (Event Streaming)" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#e1bee7;align=left;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#7b1fa2;rounded=1;strokeWidth=2;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="620" y="810" width="320" height="35" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="kafka" value="TOPIC: place.updated&#10;&#10;Partitions: 50 (key: place_id hash)&#10;Retention: 7 days&#10;Payload:&#10;  place_id: 12345&#10;  event_type: create|update|delete&#10;  timestamp: 2024-01-15T10:30:00Z&#10;  location: {lat: 12.97, lng: 77.59}&#10;  category: restaurant&#10;  name: Pizza Place&#10;&#10;Consumers:&#10;  - Indexer Service to ES bulk write&#10;  - Cache Service to Redis hot cache update&#10;  - Analytics Service to InfluxDB/ClickHouse" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f3e5f5;strokeColor=#7b1fa2;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontFamily=monospace" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="620" y="860" width="320" height="240" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="failures" value="FAILURE SCENARIOS\n\n1. Geohash boundary case:\n   Problem: Two points 50m apart on cell boundary (9q8yyzzz vs 9q8z0000) have different prefixes → single geohash query misses nearby places.\n   Solution: Query 9 cells (center + 8 neighbors). Post-filter with Haversine to get exact circle.\n\n2. Elasticsearch down:\n   Fallback: Direct PostgreSQL PostGIS query (100ms vs 50ms). Use bounding box + GIST index → still fast.\n\n3. Redis cache MISS storm (thundering herd):\n   Problem: Query result expires → 1000 concurrent requests hit Elasticsearch/PostgreSQL.\n   Solution: Lock-based cache refresh (SETNX + EX 30s lock). First request computes, others wait and retry from cache.\n\n4. Geographic sharding - large radius query:\n   Problem: User near shard boundary (SF/Oakland) queries 50km → needs both shards.\n   Solution: Add 10km overlap buffer zones. Scatter-gather to 3-5 shards, merge-sort by distance client-side.\n\n5. Real-time vs static data mismatch:\n   Problem: Uber driver moved 1km but Elasticsearch shows old location (~1-2s lag from Kafka indexing).\n   Solution: Use Redis GEOADD for real-time updates (drivers ping every 5s). Static places use PG → Kafka → ES (lag acceptable)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#ef6c00;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1040" width="1820" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

<mxCell id="analogy" value="BEGINNER ANALOGY: The data model is like a city library system. PostgreSQL PostGIS is the master ledger in the basement (ACID, every book's exact shelf location, ~10s lookup). Elasticsearch is the card catalog system (fast keyword + location search, 'find sci-fi books on the 2nd floor', ~5s). Redis GEOADD is the librarian's sticky note listing the top 100 most-borrowed books (hot cache, &lt;1s). Kafka is the overnight delivery truck that updates the card catalog when new books arrive (async sync, ~1 min lag). The GIST index is the Dewey Decimal System (spatial organization so you don't scan all shelves). Geohash boundary issue is like two books 1 inch apart on different shelves (different hash) — you check neighboring shelves too (9 cells) to find all nearby books." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e1f5fe;strokeColor=#0277bd;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1260" width="1820" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

</root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>
